            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>The Innocent Archetype is one of the three archetypes who dream of turning the world we live in into paradise, and they do so by bringing in the notion of safety.  To the Innocent, paradise is a safe world, free from evil and harm.</p>
                <p>Innocents do not yearn for freedom like the Explorer, nor do they seek paradise through understanding as the Sage does.  To the Innocent safety is everything.</p>
                <p><strong>Innocents Find Safety In Naivety</strong></p>
                <p>To attain safety, Innocent archetypes are incredibly pure and optimistic in all they do.  They are positive and always see the good in everything.  They see sunshine in the rain, every glass is full, and every cloud has a silver lining.</p>
                <p>Naive as this may seem, (Innocents are well known for their naivety), but naivety doesn’t matter to the Innocent, they are blissfully ignorant of such notions.  For it’s this naivety and exaggerated optimism that keeps them safe and brings safety into their world. </p>
                <p><strong>Purity Brings In A Safe World</strong></p>
                <p>In many ways, the Innocents optimism and pure intention does indeed start to create a safer world because they inspire others to be better people through their actions and innocence.  And the world sure would be a better place if everybody was positive and pure. </p>
                <p>The problem is, we are not all positive and pure of intention, and a world only full of positive, pure and safe intentions would also be incredibly mediocre.</p>
                <p>Problems occur for the Innocent when they experience something disappointing (something that happens often), which they cannot turn a blind eye to. Their disappointment will bring them crashing down to earth, and the fallout will be much harder on the Innocent than it would be any other archetype because of their naive outlook. </p>
                <p>So what does the Innocent do when they have experienced a disappointment?</p>
                <p>They pick themselves up, brush themselves down, file away their displeasure somewhere deep inside, smile and move on.</p>
                <p><strong>Champions of endurance</strong></p>
                <p>The Innocents endurance is off the chart because, as you can imagine, they often experience disappointment.  Innocents suffer more disappointment and have to endure more than any other archetype, all in their efforts to live in their perception of ‘safety.’</p>
                <p>Keep on reading on to find out more detailed information about how this extreme disappointment influences the Innocent over time and also to discover what other personality traits the Innocent experiences.</p>
