            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">                
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.  If we don’t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start becoming stagnant, develop poor confidence, and our wellbeing begins to deplete.</p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case of The Innocent Archetype, they attain their significance by maintaining a positive outlook.</p>
                <p>The Innocent archetype also likes to do things ‘right’.  They cannot stand punishment, either the punishment from others or of themselves (if they don’t manage to do something properly) this is also how they feel significant.</p>
                <p>Which makes some sense; if everybody did the ‘right’ thing then there would be no wrongs in the world (and it would be safe), if everybody remained positive too, then the world would be safe and happy and this to the Innocent equates to paradise. </p>
                <p><strong>Highly self-critical</strong></p>
                <p>It’s not such a positive outlook when the Innocent inevitably makes a mistake or receives criticism.  In some instances, the Innocent might be so shocked to hear that they’ve been so wrong about something, or made such a mistake that for a moment they will show their shock in their facial expressions.  They will be mortified but will quickly take it on the chin, make the necessary amendments required and move on.</p>
                <p>Too much criticism, however, could eventually bring an Innocent down.  Because it will chip away at the Innocents sense of self and esteem and could result in causing the Innocent to become nervous, clumsy, or even anxious.</p>
                <p>This is something that the Innocent would do well to look at and try to find coping strategies so that they can successfully manage the inevitable criticism that they will receive throughout life and so that it doesn’t reduce their sense of contribution or lower their esteem.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step2-back hover f-left">2. Unique Contribution</button>
