            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">                
                <p>The Innocent will often appear to be a happy go lucky character, with a childlike perspective of the world.  It’s a perspective and personality that other people adore and are often drawn to - for good and bad reasons.</p>
                <p>The Innocent is the archetype who is always smiling and enjoys the simplest things in life. They have no problem in expressing gratitude for every little thing - even the things that would seem meaningless to others.</p>
                <p><strong>A lighter outlook on life</strong></p>
                <p>Because of their light-hearted and pure approach to life, the Innocent probably doesn’t delve too deep into their internal world and will often approach life existing on the surface.  They are not the kind of archetype who would be defined as ‘deep.’  But that’s ok for them because thinking about whether they think deeply or not will not be on their radar.</p>
                <p>Innocents only ever tend to look further into themselves if they have had something to overcome; such as trauma, a painful past, or anxiety for example -  or if they have been inspired and compelled to do so.</p>
                <p>The Innocents naive perspective and adorable personality leaves them wide open for attracting people who do not approach them with respect or integrity and who probably want to take advantage of their kindness and purity in some way.  And because the Innocent is rarely realistic about the duality of life, they often walk into problems un-necessarily because they didn’t take time to think about any danger or difficulty that they might experience.</p>
                <p>Innocents only see the good in everything!</p>
                <p><strong>Easily Impressed</strong></p>
                <p>Innocents are easily impressed, they take great delight in everything, which makes them wonderful company as long as you don’t want to get into any gritty conversations.  They enjoy the simplest of things and will be delighted to do many things that most other people would feel unimpressed by, or even put out by.</p>
                <p>Let’s just say that an Innocent archetype is an inexpensive date.  Although they’d probably be delighted with something fabulous too, it would just be lost on the Innocent a little bit because they don't understand why there needs to be so many bells and whistles to experience a good time when you can breathe in some fresh air and enjoy some great company to do that! </p>
                <p><strong>Finds Joy In Simplicity</strong></p>
                <p>Innocent archetypes love the simple life, they are patient, undemanding and a pleasure to be around.  They don’t tend to live extravagant lifestyles, not because they don’t have the money too (although that’s likely to be the case) but because they don’t need to, and they don’t want a big pile of unnecessary stuff or pretentious experiences.   In relationships, they are loving and patient, only requiring the same love and patience back.</p>
                <p><strong>Money Is Not Important</strong></p>
                <p>Money is not something that is important to an Innocent archetype. If they have money, they’ve probably come about it unexpectedly either through inheritance, a wealthy family or by accidentally earning a lot because they are doing something they love.  If the Innocent does have money, they probably don’t spend it though, and most Innocents are likely to have some savings squirreled away somewhere too.</p>
                <p>Innocent archetypes don’t find any joy in attaining financial wealth, but when it comes to finding happiness, that’s everything for them.</p>
                <p><strong>Maintain A Balanced Life</strong></p>
                <p>Innocent archetypes tend to lead a balanced and active life.  They make a point of eating healthily, taking the daily recommended dose of exercise, vitamins or meditation (whatever they deem or have learned is essential for their health).  They appear to be emotionally balanced (and for the most part they are) and live a very holistic lifestyle.</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even From Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side, Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it’s discussed in great detail, concerning your dominant archetype in the premium reports.  There is a hidden side, or an unconscious life (to be more precise) that we experience internally but we don’t, or can't show or express to the world, and there’s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to us.  </p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these aspects of our ‘self,’ we begin to learn about what is really driving us.  We begin to discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don’t do the things that we want to do, or should do). And we can start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires, or reach our full potential.  </p>
                <p>In the case of The Innocent archetype, their hidden personality traits often lie in understanding the reasons why they need to do everything ‘right’, and why they feel ‘punished’ when they do something wrong.</p>
                <p>Most driving factors for an Innocent will originate from deep and limiting beliefs that are pushing their ideas forward into their life and have a significant influence on the way that they think. Mostly what they are doing is bringing their fear of punishment to their reality so that they can realize that there is something wrong and develop the coping skills to correct that (it’s just unfortunate that the Innocent often doesn’t notice this pattern).</p>
                <p>If they did notice the pattern and made the necessary changes they need to make, it won’t mean that the Innocent will lose their ability to remain positive or to do things as well as they do.</p>
