            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">                
                <p><strong>Happiness Is A Priority For The Innocent</strong></p>
                <p>Everyone seeks happiness in some way. Some often tie it to a specific thing, but for the Innocent, happiness is related to everything.  Being present in the moment is not hard for the Innocent, in fact, it’s probably a habit.  They’ll stop to smell the roses, embrace the seasons and delight in other people's happiness as much as their own (even if they are unhappy at the time).</p>
                <p><strong>Has ‘Bounce Back’ Ability</strong></p>
                <p>Because of the Innocent’s positive but naive nature, they often have to pick themselves up from stumbles and falls, and they do so, quite easily.</p>
                <p>This ‘bounce-back-ability’ makes them reliable, a pleasure to be around and resistant to many of life's challenges.  But it also makes them naive and doesn’t encourage them to stop and ring the changes so that they don’t walk into the same problem again.</p>
                <p>Chances are an Innocent will repeat mistakes frequently because they won’t dwell on the situation enough to realize that they could avoid the situation.   However, if somebody has specifically told an Innocent they are making a mistake they’ll correct it in a heartbeat and will probably never repeat that mistake ever again.</p>
                <p><strong>Knows How To Live A Balanced Lifestyle</strong></p>
                <p>Most of us have to work hard at maintaining a balanced lifestyle but not the Innocent archetype. They’ll have it down to a tee and will undoubtedly appear to be perfect in comparison to other people.</p>
                <p><strong>Is Pleasurable Company</strong></p>
                <p>It will be hard not to enjoy the company of an Innocent - they exude joy and appreciation in all that they do, and they also love to celebrate other people’s happiness too.  But if you want a deep conversation or to do something that is not simple or safe then you’d be better off finding a different friend for those types of conversations and experiences.</p>
                <p><strong>Will Be A Loyal And Reliable Worker</strong></p>
                <p>The Innocents fear of punishment will ensure that they will be meticulous in their work.  They will also be extremely loyal and reliable.  They’d make great Personal Assistants and Accountability Coaches because of this trait although they won’t be dynamic, or creative with ideas.  But that doesn’t matter because every business would thrive with a few Innocents working there mixed amongst the Creators and Hero’s!</p>
                
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Does Not Know How To Self Assert</strong></p>
                <p>Innocent archetypes don’t like to shake up the status quo, they don’t like to let people down, and their deep fear of punishment makes it very difficult for the Innocent Archetype to be able to find the courage, or inclination to assert themselves.</p>
                <p>Instead, they will agree to most things (even if they don’t want to do or experience those things) and won’t usually speak up if somebody is taking advantage of them.  This often leads to having to do things that they don’t want to do or allowing people to push them around or to take advantage of them.</p>
                <p><strong>Can Be Perceived As Boring Or Mundane</strong></p>
                <p>The Innocents love for sticking to rules, routines, and other people's boundaries along with their desire for a healthy life and joyful perspective can make them seem boring or mundane to other people.  Innocents tend not to have too much grit or depth.</p>
                <p>Instead, they glow with purity and positivity which is not always enough to capture the attention of those around them.</p>
                <p><strong>Views The World From A Biased Perspective</strong></p>
                <p>You could say that the Innocent is one of the archetypes who tends to see the world through rose-colored glasses - because it would certainly seem that way.  The reality is that they don’t necessarily see the world this way, they just choose to ignore all of the bad stuff and discount any problems.</p>
                <p>If they stopped to think about things, they know all of this undesirable ‘stuff’ is out there they don’t want to look at it which means that they often have a skewed perception of the world.</p>
                <p>Critical thinking is also not the Innocent’s forte, not at all because they only look for the good which can lead to just one thing - walking into problems.</p>
                <p><strong>Believe That Their Morals Are The Only Way</strong></p>
                <p>Innocents have strong morals. They also have a strong sense of what is right and what is wrong along with high expectations that everybody also has the same morals and understands right from wrong according to the Innocents perception of that.</p>
                <p>Of course, we all have ideas of some things that we would never do that others think is ok to do and if our opinions don't match up to the Innocent’s perspective, they’ll probably be surprised and secretly disappointed.</p>
                <p><strong>Are Frequent Prey To Deception</strong></p>
                <p>Because the Innocent does not participate in critical thinking at all and has a skewed bias on how the world should be, they often don’t notice when somebody is trying to deceive them.  It’s almost certain that an Innocent is one of the archetypes who are deceived and let down by others the most.</p>
