            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">                
                <p>Innocents focus on the good things always and easily pick themselves up from a fall. The problem is that the Innocent will experience many falls because they have such an idealistic and unrealistic perspective on the world that they find disappointment around every corner.</p>
                <p>And when they encounter disappointment, an Innocent will probably just keep on keeping on without stopping to process their feelings, instead choosing to bury them, in the hope that they will go away.</p>
                <p><strong>Innocents Need to Address Their Repressed Feelings</strong></p>
                <p>Repressed feelings, however, do not go away.  Instead, these feelings will keep finding opportunities to present themselves to the Innocent so that they might be reconciled.</p>
                <p>The example above shows how the unconscious mind processes energy. Repressed emotion and memories use up a lot of data and so when there is not enough space for any more emotion the unconscious mind will start to re-present the emotion so that the person involved can reconcile it.</p>
                <p>If this emotion is not reconciled, it will eventually cause problems such as some form of emotional overwhelm or even anxiety, depression, panic attacks or illness.</p>
                <p>None of these situations will be ideal for the Innocent to experience - far from it.</p>
                <p>Innocents cannot stand to feel unsafe, and they fear punishment and failure too, so in many cases, if they were to experience the issues highlighted above, they’d inevitably have to take some time away from their obligations and would probably feel as though they were letting people down.</p>
                <p>This will trigger their fear of punishment and failure and in turn will require more endurance (which was the cause of the problem in the first place!)</p>
                <p>And because the Innocent hates to be punished and so often toes the line and abides by rules and codes, they will beat themselves up if they have to break a code or rule because of being unwell.</p>
                <p><strong>Irony of the Innocent</strong></p>
                <p>All of these problems would be unnecessary if the Innocent could face their greatest challenge which is to protect themselves and take a realistic view of the world (how ironic it is that an archetype who advocates safety and optimism with every fiber of their being has to protect themselves and get real!). </p>
                <p>Most archetypes have one great conflict where they need to balance out opposites to attain their goals.  The innocent needs to understand that nothing in this world is perfect and that growing means learning from our own mistakes. Their misconception of it being a form of punishment prevents them from realizing its value – an excellent opportunity to develop themselves.</p>
                <p>And if the Innocent could start to take a slightly more in-depth look at how they experience the world and learn to be more assertive and protective of themselves, they can bring themselves down to earth and open their eyes to the imperfections of it.</p>
                <p>They can then set realistic boundaries - which means that they won’t be so disappointed so frequently, and they will need to endure less because they won’t have as many problems.  </p>
                <p>An Innocent needs to learn that we can’t have safety without realism and practicality and then they should do everything they can to introduce these qualities into their lives.  If they succeed, they will experience safety in a way that they probably didn’t even think existed, despite their optimism.</p>
                <p><strong>How An Innocent Archetype Can Master Their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>As an Innocent starts to understand the secrets behind their greatest challenge and learn to develop critical strategies for experiencing the world they will reap the rewards and bring sustainable safety and joy into their lives without any of the endurance.</p>
                <p>Because all of their strengths will be balanced, the Innocent will learn how to maintain such without sabotaging their sense of joy and safety.</p>
                <p>If you are an Innocent, you can learn more about how to do this in the Premium Archetype Reports.</p>
